-- title:
--   Integral twisted commutant closed under ring operations
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by the integer powers of $\sigma$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with completion $K_v$, let $c$ be a unit of $K_v$, and let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Assume `IsNormOf` holds for the scalar matrix $c$ and $\delta$, i.e. the image under `toTensorGL` of the scalar matrix with entry $c$ is conjugate, in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$, to `normString K L (v.adicCompletion K) σ δ`; and assume that $\delta$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate to any scalar: for no unit $z$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ is there $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ with $\mathrm{scalar}(z) = x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)$, where $\sigma$ acts on matrices entrywise through `sigmaTensor`, the map $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$. Let $O$ be the set of $2\times 2$ matrices $x$ over $L \otimes_K K_v$ with $x\delta = \delta\, x^{\sigma}$ (entrywise `sigmaTensor`) and such that either $x = 0$ or $\det x = 1 \otimes s$ for some unit $s$ of $K_v$ with $\mathrm{v}(s) \le 1$. Then $0 \in O$, $1 \in O$, and $O$ is closed under addition, negation and multiplication, and under multiplication by $1 \otimes a$ for every $a$ in the valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$ of $K_v$.
--
--   At a place of the second kind the twisted commutant of $\delta$ is a division quaternion algebra over $K_v$ with reduced norm given by the determinant, and the statement says that its subset of elements of integral reduced norm is an $\mathcal{O}_v$-order; the substance is the ultrametric behaviour of the reduced norm, which gives closure under addition. It is used in the computation of the local covolume of the twisted centralizer at such places.
